  before                             after                         nodes
  ((2 * 3) + (x * (4 + 1)))          (6 + (x * 5))           9 ->  5  (  44% gone)
  ((1 + 2) * (10 - 4))               18                      7 ->  1  (  86% gone)
  (y + z)                            (y + z)                 3 ->  3  (   0% gone)
  (1 / 0)                            (1 / 0)                 3 ->  3  (   0% gone)

=== Does folding need a second pass? ===
  (1 + (2 + (3 + 4)))
  after one pass:  10  (nodes 7 -> 1)
  after two passes: 10
  Because fold() recurses into the children BEFORE testing the parent,
  one bottom-up pass already reaches a fixed point here.
